      lab: "Trace an HTTP route from host/path to its Service and list the dependencies you would verify before changing policy.",
      mistakes: ["Assuming Kubernetes automatically provides an Ingress controller.", "Writing a policy with the wrong namespace or Pod selector.", "Assuming a NetworkPolicy is enforced by a CNI that does not support it."],
      exam: "Follow the chain from listener to route to Service to endpoints; then check policy. Do not diagnose HTTP routing from Pod readiness alone.",
      questions: [quiz("What makes an Ingress resource effective?", ["An installed controller that implements it", "A ConfigMap named ingress", "A PodDisruptionBudget", "An etcd snapshot"], 0, "The Ingress object is declarative; a controller implements the data plane.")],
      summary: ["NetworkPolicy needs CNI enforcement.", "Ingress needs a controller.", "Gateway API separates infrastructure attachment from route rules."]
